YOLO (You Only Look Once)
YOLO (You Only Look Once) is a deep learning model used for real-time object detection.
It detects and classifies multiple objects in images and videos.
It processes the image using a single pass through the network, making it very fast.
It generates bounding boxes around detected objects.
It assigns class labels such as person, car, bike, dog, or traffic signal.
It can detect multiple objects simultaneously in a single image.
It is widely used in CCTV surveillance systems.
It is used in traffic monitoring to detect vehicles and pedestrians.
It helps self-driving cars identify obstacles and road objects.
It is used in smart parking systems to count and track vehicles.
It is commonly applied in security, robotics, and industrial automation.
YOLO is known for its high speed and real-time performance.
It is one of the most popular and widely used object detection models in Deep Learning.

